WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
Two new products go on
sale on the same day.

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.050
One starts with a high price,

3
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.150
and the maker cuts it later.

4
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:11.090
The other starts cheap, and the
maker raises the price later.

5
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.310
Both firms want to make a profit.

6
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.690
So why do some new
products launch at a high

7
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.430
price while others start out cheap?

8
00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.630
In this mission, you'll
meet six pricing strategies,

9
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:26.190
from cost-plus to psychological,
and work out a price with a mark-up.

10
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.660
Then you'll test in a
graph lab whether cutting

11
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.420
a price brings in more money or less.

12
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.080
Your mission: find out what
decides a launch price.
